<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Japanese, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    Polite です/ます in sentences; short nouns and verb stems on buttons and labels. Japanese has one plural form
    (other), so each plural has only that one. "Vehicle" is 車両; "run" is 便 (a timetabled departure, "6:43発の便",
    "1503便"); "trip" is 運行 (運行開始, 運行終了, 運行を再開); "report" is 送信, counted in 件 ("142件送信"), and a
    saved report is 位置; "dispatcher" is 運行管理者; "block" is 運用; "route" is 路線; "stop" is 停留所; "agency" is
    事業者; "driver" is 運転士; "riders" is 乗客; "schedule" and "timetable" are 時刻表; "phone" is スマートフォン;
    "diagnostics" is 診断情報. Half-width spaces set Latin text and placeholders for names and numbers apart
    ("路線 %1$s", "GPS なし"), but not counts from their counters ("%1$d分遅れ").
-->
